
# CSIT314 Progress Report 
**Event Management System**  

---

## 1. Project Overview
This group project involves the design and development of an Event Management System, intended to simulate platforms like Eventbrite or Humanitix. The application will allow general users to register and log in, browse events, purchase tickets, and receive notifications. Event organisers will be able to create and manage events, view attendees, and access basic analytics and payment features.

The system is being developed as part of the CSIT314 Systems Development Methodologies subject and follows an iterative development lifecycle with agile practices integrated throughout the semester.

---

## 2. Development Methodology
After evaluating multiple project management models, the group adopted **Scrum** due to its structured sprint planning, suitability for collaborative workflows, and alignment with the semester schedule. Scrum encourages regular feedback and short delivery cycles, which is appropriate for the practical nature of the system and frequent deliverables.

### Sprint Calendar
| Sprint | Dates            | Focus                                                                 |
|--------|------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| 1      | Apr 1 – Apr 12   | Finalise user stories, assign roles, set up GitHub repo, UI mockups     |
| 2      | Apr 15 – Apr 26  | Backend setup, frontend login/register, define UML diagrams             |
| 3      | Apr 29 – May 10  | Event listing, event creation, registration functionality               |
| 4      | May 13 – May 24  | Notifications, payment mock logic, organiser dashboard features         |
| 5      | May 27 – May 31  | Testing, UI polishing, responsiveness fixes                             |
| 6      | Jun 3 – Jun 7    | Finalise user manual, full documentation, final deployment              |

### Tools Used
- **GitHub Projects** – Task tracking, sprint planning, documentation versioning
- **GitHub Actions** – CI/CD pipeline (planned integration)
- **Node.js (Express)** – Backend framework
- **HTML/CSS/JS** – Frontend (to be integrated)
- **Figma** – UI wireframes and mockups (initial stage)

